eness; ring-count / heavy-atom / Fsp3 / rotatable-bond distributions; **long-chain over-representation detector** (longest linear carbon chain distribution, fraction beyond reference q99, alkyl-only/\"fatty-acid-like\" fraction, aur cLogP-gain ka kitna hissa sirf chain-length inflation se aata hai \u2014 regression-based attribution); LE (lipophilicity efficiency).\n\n**E. Real-world distribution alignment:** reference corpora **ChEMBL** (bioactive/drug-like), **PCBA-like high-throughput screening set**, aur **GDB/Enamine-REAL-like makeable space**; tests \u2014 per-descriptor **KS** (MW, cLogP, HBA/HBD, TPSA, rotatable bonds, ring counts, longest chain), histogram **Wasserstein/EMD**, **MMD** with Tanimoto/GIN kernel (generated vs corpus), scaffold-frequency **JSD/KL**, aur quantile-calibration (central-95% support ke andar fraction). Multi-comparison correction (BH/Holm), bootstrap CIs, effect sizes (Cliff's delta).\n\n**F. Target-specific enrichment & \"hallucination\" battery:** docking-score distribution + hit fractions, cross-target selectivity agar panel ho; **\"target-agnostic repeats\"** metric (alag targets par same high-affinity scaffolds = hallucinated affinity ka evidence); **surrogate\u2192independent-rescoring transfer gap**; out-of-support fraction. Yahi \"molecular hallucination\" ki operational multi-component paribhasha hogi (valence-invalid | synthesability-undefined | target-agnostic repeats | distributionally out-of-support).\n\n**G. Statistics/feasibility:** \u22653\u20135 paired seeds, fixed scaffold-split test set, pre-registered primary endpoint (proposed: *valid \u2227 novel \u2227 makeable \u2227 within-reference-support fraction, conditional on internal diversity \u2265 ~0.85\u00d7 baseline*), bootstrap/permutation tests, per-arm compute estimates (docking call count, CPU-hours), CPU-only docking budget ko design me hi cap kiya jayega.\n\n---\n\n## 3) Assumptions & uncertainties \u2014 researcher se clarification chahiye (6 topics)\n1. *