**Reference corpora \u2014 do regimes (design feature; ambiguity chhupi nahi):**\n- **R-BIO:** bioactive/drug-like (ChEMBL-like, activity-annotated).\n- **R-MK:** makeable/purchasable (Enamine-REAL-like / GDB-style enumerated makeable space).\n- **Primary alignment regime = R-BIO** (pre-specified, kyunki sawaal \"targeted molecule discovery\" ke baare me hai). R-MK **secondary + interaction** role: lipophilicity/chain-length par expectations opposite hain (chain inflation R-BIO par artifact, R-MK par legitimate space), isliye har artifact verdict **regime-conditional** report hoga, aur \"regime-dependent artifact inversion\" ek first-class reported outcome hai, confound nahi.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Arms aur controls\n\n**Primary factor (stated assumption, confirmed source fact nahi): feedback injection point** \u2014 *E1* training-time (RL reward / TB-loss reweighting, KL-to-reference \u03b2 ke saath) \u00b7 *E2* inference-time (value-guided beam / annealed resample; weights frozen) \u00b7 *E3* hybrid.\n\n| Arm | Content | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A0** | No-feedback pretrained baseline (+ KL anchor) | Reference policy; diversity/alignment anchor |\n| **A1** | Single-property feedback: {cLogP, QED, SA, affinity} \u00d7 {E1,E2,E3} (12 configs) | Component contributions, shortcut detection |\n| **A2** | Full multi-property feedback (fixed weights), mid \u03b2, constant schedule, E1/E2/E3 | Main \"full feedback\" effect |\n| **A3** | \u03b2 sweep {0.03, 0.1, 0.3, 1.0} (mid = A2) \u00d7 E1/E2/E3 | Feedback-strength tradeoff curve |\n| **A4** | Schedule {constant, linear ramp, warmup-hold, anneal, curriculum QED\u2192SA\u2192affinity} \u00d7 E1/E3 | Feedback schedule |\n| **A5** | Diversity-preserving feedback: (i) intra-batch ECFP4 dissimilarity repulsion, (ii) quality-diversity islands / constrained Pareto (diversity as constraint) \u00d7 E1/E3 | \"feedback helps\" **vs** \"feedback + diversity mechanism helps\" ka separation |\n| **A6** | **Post-hoc top-k filter on A0 samples, output count exactly matched** to feedback-arm output (composite-score ranking) | Truncation-vs-distribution-shift control (load-bearing) |\n| **A7** | Placebo: shuffled-reward + identity-reward | Content-specificity control |\n| **A8** | Docking-in-loop (Vina as inner-loop reward, small budget) | Surrogate-fidelity upper reference |\n| **X-PANEL** | Optional: A2/A5 on a 2\u20134 target panel | target-agnostic-repeat hallucination metric |\n\n**Scale (proposed planning arithmetic, ek consistency script se \u2014 benchmark nahi):** 39 training configs \u00d7 seeds (5 primary / 3 sweep) = **161 training runs** + **10 eval-only A6 conditions** = **171 evaluation conditions**; ~**7.6M** generator forward-outputs (E2 arms ka 10\u00d7 oversampling included); docking audit tier = 13 configs \u00d7 3 seeds = 39 runs \u00d7 1,000 ligands = **39,000 dockings + 39,000 rescorings**; ~**3,864 KS tests** (12 descriptors \u00d7 161 runs \u00d7 2 regimes) \u2192 multiple-testing correction anivarya; 322 MMD comparisons (2,000\u00d72,000 kernel subsample).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Metrics battery\n\n**(a) Validity / valence (H2 primary):** RDKit sanitization pass rate, per-error-class valence-failure counts, SMILES parse/canonicalization success, disconnected-fragment (\".\") rate.\n\n**(b) Property scores (H1):** QED, cLogP, MW, TPSA, HBA/HBD, rotatable bonds, SA score, **Lipophilicity Efficiency (LE = cLogP/heavy-atom count)**, target-tier: Vina score + independent rescoring. **Composite property score** pre-specified: `0.4\u00b7QED_norm + 0.3\u00b7(1\u2212SA_norm) + 0.3\u00b7affinity_norm` (weights = proposed design parameters; univariate results separately reported as secondaries).\n\n**(c) Diversity (H3):** **internal diversity** = mean pairwise 1\u2212Tanimoto (ECFP4, r=2); **scaffold diversity** = unique Bemis\u2013Murcko scaffolds per 1k, effective scaffold number (exp(entropy)), scaffold-frequency Gini; ECFP4 distinct-mer count; top-1000-pairs self-overlap; nearest-neighbor-Tanimoto histogram (train vs generated).\n\n**(d) Structural-artifact / long-chain detector (regime-conditional):** longest **linear carbon-chain length** distribution; fraction with chain > reference-corpus **q99**; alkyl-only/\"fatty-acid-like\" fraction (sp3-carbon fraction > threshold \u2227 ring count = 0); chain-length\u2194cLogP coupling slope; **cLogP-gain attribution (mediation) regression** \u2014 total cLogP gain ka kitna hissa sirf chain-length inflation + heavy-atom count hai (pre-specified). **Verdict rule:** artifact flagged **only relative to the regime used as reference** (R-BIO par chain-inflation penalty active; R-MK par wahi molecules out-of-support nahi hongi \u2192 inversion reported).\n\n**(e) \"Molecular hallucination\" \u2014 4-component operational battery:**\n- **PRIMARY (per researcher resolution 3):** **H-P1 out-of-reference-support** (support = union of R-BIO central-95% quantile bands on 12 descriptors; Mahalanobis-outlier test in descriptor space) **+ H-P2 valence/sanitization invalid**.\n- **SECONDARY/exploratory:** **H-S1 synthesability-undefined/unmakeable** (SA > threshold, non-sanitizable after tautomer canonicalization, unmakeability flag); **H-S2 target-agnostic repeats** (same/near-duplicate scaffold high-affinity across unrelated targets \u2014 fully defined only under X-PANEL).\n- **MANDATORY reward-hacking diagnostic:** **surrogate\u2192independent-rescoring transfer gap** = (surrogate-predicted affinity gain) \u2212 (Vina + independent-rescoring affinity gain). Agar surrogate gain bina real gain ke \u2192 N-hacking supported, H1 **fails** chahe reward kitna bhi improve ho.\n\n**(f) Distribution alignment (H3), per regime:** per-descriptor **KS** D + p; histogram **Wasserstein-1/EMD**; **MMD** (ECFP4-Tanimoto kernel ek, GIN-embedding kernel dusra) with permutation p; **JSD/KL** on scaffold-frequency distribution; **quantile-calibration** = fraction inside reference central-95% band (per descriptor); \"realism\" discriminator AUC (generated-vs-corpus, cross-validated) \u2014 lower AUC = better alignment.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Endpoints\n\n**PRIMARY joint endpoint (pre-registered, single scalar per arm\u00d7seed) \u2014 \"Qualified-Hit Fraction with diversity floor\" (QHF-DF):**\n```\nQHF-DF = 0                                            if ID(arm) < f_div \u00b7 ID(A0)      [diversity floor gate]\n       = fraction of generated molecules that are valid \u2227 novel (NN-Tanimoto < 0.4 to train)\n         \u2227 in-R-BIO-support \u2227 composite \u2265 \u03c4_c         otherwise\n```\n`f_div = 0.85`, `\u03c4_c` = pilot-A0 se frozen composite cut \u2014 **dono pre-registered proposed design parameters**. Ye joint construction isliye, kyunki property-only metric truncation/mode-collapse ko reward kar dega. **Sensitivity (added after a logic check of the gate):** f_div \u2208 {0.70, 0.80, 0.85, 0.90}; ek fixed floor A5-jaisi arms ko artificially zero kar sakta hai jabki diversity loss genuine tradeoff hai, isliye primary verdict f_div-sweep ke under report hoga (robustness = same sign across floors) aur gated arms ka raw composite bhi reported hoga.\n\n**Key secondaries (pre-registered):** (S1) composite property score; (S2) hallucination primary components (H-P1, H-P2); (S3) internal + scaffold diversity; (S4) per-regime KS/MMD/calibration; (S5) long-chain artifact fraction per regime; (S6) transfer gap (reward-hacking diagnostic).\n\n**Pre-registered decision matrix:** H1 supported = A2 > A0 *and* A2 > A6 *and* transfer gap > 0. H3 supported = A2/A5 alignment better than A0 on R-BIO *and* ID \u2265 floor *and* long-chain artifact fraction not increased on R-BIO. H2 supported = hallucination primary rate lower than A0 **and than A7-placebo**. \"Feedback embedding (not filtering)\" ki claim tabhi supported jab A2 > A6 by pre-set margin \u2014 A6, E1-vs-E2 comparison se bhi stronger single control hai.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Analysis plan\n\n- **Seeds/pairing:** 5 seeds (primary arms), 3 (sweeps); same seed set across arms (paired design). Scaffold-disjoint train/test split aur evaluation reference sets sab arms ke liye fixed (seed-independent data).\n- **Inference:** paired-seed contrasts \u2192 **stratified permutation / Wilcoxon** (n=5 par parametric t nahi), effect size **Cliff's delta**; **bootstrap 95% CIs** (10k resamples; diversity metrics par scaffold-stratified resampling taaki pseudoreplication na ho).\n- **Multiple testing:** **Holm\u2013Bonferroni within each endpoint family**, **BH-FDR q=0.05** across the ~3,864-test descriptor battery; post-hoc tuning se bachne ke liye primary endpoint ek hi hai, baaki sab pre-declared secondary.\n- **Trend analysis:** \u03b2-sweep par monotonicity/isotonic check; **\u03b2_crit** = maximum \u03b2 jahan ID \u2265 floor (interpreted tradeoff, pre-specified); schedule \u00d7 \u03b2 interaction test.\n- **Mediation:** property/cLogP gain \u2192 chain-length + heavy-atom mediation; **artifact-adjusted property gain** report (artifact contribution subtract karke).\n- **Pareto reporting (mandatory):** har arm\u00d7seed (property, diversity, alignment) 3-D space me; **dominance relations + Pareto front per regime**; single scalar ke alawa sawaal \"kya koi feedback arm A0 ko teeno axes par Pareto-dominates karta hai?\" \u2014 sabse honest answer, aur single-metric failure ko expose karta hai.\n- **Attribution summary:** component (A1) \u00d7 injection (E1/E2/E3) \u00d7 \u03b2 \u00d7 schedule ka factorial-effect table, A7-placebo ke\u5bf9\u7167 differences ke saath.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Feasibility (CPU-only reality se honest tie) + required external provisions\n\n**Observed environment (verified):** `/workspace` me sirf `task.json`; **RDKit/Vina/Open Babel/numpy/torch sab missing**; **network blocked** (DNS fail); **no GPU**; 224 CPU cores, ~2 TB RAM. \u2192 Design isi environment me executable nahi hai; neeche ki provisions ise resolve karti hain (isliye design \"infeasible in this environment\" nahi dikhega bina bataye).\n\n**Budget-limiting tiers (proposed planning arithmetic, benchmarked nahi):**\n1. **Training (dominant cost):** ~**1,000\u20133,900 core-hours** for 161 runs; CPU-only \u2248 **60\u2013240 h wall** at 16-way parallelism. \u2192 Mitigation: **pre-registered \"must-run core\" subset** (~32 runs: A0, A1-{QED,affinity}, A2\u00d73, A3 mid/high \u03b2, A5\u00d72, A6\u00d72, A7\u00d72, A8\u00d71) taaki budget contraction pre-planned ho, post-hoc nahi.\n2. **Docking audit (224 cores par limiting NAHI):** 39,000 dockings + 39,000 rescorings @ ~2 s = **~22 core-hours \u2248 ~6 min wall** at full core count; ligand prep (tautomer/protonation/3D embed) 2\u20135\u00d7 overhead dega. **Ceiling: \u2264 60,000 docking calls study-wide**; A8 docking-in-loop ke liye alag **\u2264 5,000** cap (single receptor, pre-computed grid).\n3. **Descriptor/fingerprint scoring:** RDKit par SA non-trivial \u2192 SA precompute + cache, descriptors 32-way sharded; hours-scale, non-limiting.\n4. **MMD/KS battery:** 322 MMD comparisons, 2,000\u00d72,000 fixed-seed subsample \u2192 hours-scale, non-limiting.\n\n**Required external provisions (consolidated; in-workspace available NAHI):**\n1. **Software env:** RDKit (+Mordred), Open Babel, AutoDock Vina/smina, numpy/scipy/pandas/scikit-learn, torch, PyG \u2014 **pinned versions** (Vina scores versions ke beech unstable hote hain \u2192 version lock + fixed poses par rescoring).\n2. **Generator code + checkpoints**, ya public training corpus (ZINC-like) se pretrain ka budget.\n3. **Reference corpora:** ChEMBL-like bioactive set (R-BIO) + Enamine-REAL-like/GDB-style makeable set (R-MK), license-cleared.\n4. **Receptor structure + prepared binding-site grid** (single target) + docking config; optional panel ke liye 2\u20134 targets.\n5. **Trained affinity surrogate** + ek **independent** scoring function (transfer-gap diagnostic ke liye non-negotiable).\n6. SA-score contribution tables, ECFP4/GIN embedding assets, aur \"must-run core\" ko cover karta hua compute allocation.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Open clarifications, apnaye gaye defaults ke saath (assumption vs brief-se-fixed)\n\n| # | Open clarification | **Adopted default** | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Docking budget; single vs panel target | Audit-only docking \u226460k calls; **single receptor**; panel = optional X-PANEL | Assumption (panel-optional = researcher resolution 4) |\n| 2 | Surrogate vs oracle in loop; refresh allowed? | Surrogate in loop (static), **2 refresh checkpoints** ka A2-variant; A8 = docking-in-loop | Assumption |\n| 3 | Mandated injection point? | **Not fixed \u2192 primary factor E1/E2/E3** | Assumption (researcher resolution 1) |\n| 4 | Model family / checkpoints / generation budget | GFlowNet-TB + RL-Transformer, \u226450M, 10k molecules/run | Assumption |\n| 5 | Hallucination primary component | **H-P1 out-of-support + H-P2 valence = primary**; H-S1/H-S2 secondary; transfer gap **mandatory** | Adopted per researcher resolution 3 |\n| 6 | \"Real-world\" = drug-like ya makeable? | **R-BIO primary, R-MK secondary + regime-interaction analysis** | Adopted per researcher resolution 2 |\n| 7 | Diversity floor value (self-raised) | f_div = 0.85 primary + {0.70, 0.80, 0.85, 0.90} sensitivity | Design-parameter assumption (gate-logic check ke baad added) |\n\n**Fixed by brief/task:** property set (p-logP, QED, binding affinity); diversity preservation aur long-chain over-representation avoidance; real-world-distribution alignment; design-only constraint (\"do not claim that an experiment was run\"); koi dataset/codebase provided nahi.\n**Assumptions (fixed nahi):** upar ki table ke rows 1\u20134, \u00a72 ke model/target/corpora choices, saare numeric thresholds, CPU-viability estimates.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Known design weaknesses (self-reported)\n(i) **CPU-only me RL fine-tuning dominant cost** hai \u2192 reduced-seed contraction pre-registered. (ii) **Vina ka score real binding free energy nahi** \u2192 affinity component \"predicted affinity\" hi rahega; transfer gap isko partially guard karta hai, poora nahi. (iii) **f_div gate A5 ko artificially penalize kar sakta hai** \u2192 sensitivity sweep added. (iv) **Surrogate-exploitation puri tarah eliminate nahi**, sirf measurable. (v) **Corpus composition hi \"artifact\" ki paribhasha badal deta hai** (regime inversion) \u2192 isliye dual-regime mandatory.\n", "evidence": "REPOSITORY / ENVIRONMENT OBSERVATIONS (design-only session; exploratory checks only, no experiment run):\n1. `ls -la /workspace` + `find /workspace -maxdepth 2 -type f` -> ONLY `task.json` (794 B). No codebase, notebooks, configs, datasets, or on-disk `track.md`.\n2. `cat /workspace/task.json` -> `\"documents\": {\"track.md\": \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"}`, `\"datasets\": []`, `\"gpu_enabled\": false`, network disabled. Confirms design-only scope and zero provided assets.\n3. Import probe (rdkit, openbabel, numpy, torch, torch_geometric, transformers, vina, scipy, pandas, sklearn, seaborn, matplotlib, dm_tree, tensorflow, ray, gym) -> ALL MISSING; Python 3.14.4; `pip list` shows only unrelated system packages (ansible, cryptography, Jinja2...). No cheminformatics/QA stack.\n4. `which obabel vina smina gnina openbabel` -> none found; no conda/uv/pip.\n5. Filesystem scan (`*.sdf, *.smi, *.pdb, *.cif, *chembl*, *vina*, *.ckpt, *.safetensors` over `/ -xdev`) -> ZERO hits: no receptor/target structures, no checkpoints, no molecular corpora.\n6. Network probe `socket.create_connection(('pypi.org',443))` -> `NET BLOCKED gaierror ... Temporary failure in name resolution`; no package/corpora/checkpoint download possible in-session.\n7. `nproc` -> 224; `free -g` -> ~2011 GB RAM total. High CPU parallelism, no GPU.\n\nBUDGET / CONSISTENCY ARITHMETIC (planning script; NOT a benchmark or experiment):\n- Arm grid -> 39 training configs x seeds (5 primary / 3 sweep) = 161 training runs; + 10 eval-only A6 conditions = 171 evaluation conditions; ~7.61M generator forward-outputs (incl. 10x inference-time oversampling for E2 arms).\n- Docking audit tier -> 13 configs x 3 seeds = 39 runs x 1,000 ligands = 39,000 dockings + 39,000 rescorings; at 2 s/call = 21.7 core-hours -> 5.8 min wall on 224 cores. Conclusion: docking is NOT the limiting tier; training is.\n- Training planning estimate -> 966-3,864 core-hours single-core; 60-242 h wall at 16-way parallel CPU. This motivated the pre-registered \"must-run core\" (~32-run) contraction.\n- Multiple-testing load -> 12 descriptors x 161 runs x 2 regimes = 3,864 KS tests; 322 MMD comparisons at 2,000x2,000 subsample. Justifies Holm/BH correction as an a-priori design requirement rather than an afterthought.\n\nJOINT-ENDPOINT LOGIC CHECK (validation of the proposed primary metric's logic, not data analysis):\nImplemented the QHF-DF gate (qualified = valid AND novel AND in-support AND composite>=tau, forced to 0 if internal diversity < f_div x baseline) on illustrative synthetic inputs. Output: baseline 0.03; diversity-collapsing arm (ID 0.78 vs floor 0.697) = 0.42; diversity-mechanism arm (ID 0.71) = 0.26; truncation-only filtered arm (ID 0.41) = 0.00. Findings: (a) the gate does correctly zero the matched-count post-hoc-filter control, confirming it can separate distribution shift from truncation, which is exactly the load-bearing claim; (b) the same gate can zero out arms with a modest genuine diversity loss if f_div is set too high -> design updated with a pre-registered f_div sensitivity sweep {0.70, 0.80, 0.85, 0.90} plus mandatory raw-composite reporting for gated arms (also recorded as design weakness iii and uncertainty 5).", "assumptions": ["Feedback injection point (training-time vs inference-time vs hybrid) is NOT a source-confirmed requirement; it is the primary experimental factor, labeled as a stated assumption (researcher resolution 1).", "'Real-world distribution' is operationalized as two regimes: R-BIO (ChEMBL-like bioactive) as the pre-specified PRIMARY alignment reference and R-MK (Enamine-REAL/GDB-like makeable) as secondary plus regime-interaction analysis; long-chain artifact verdicts are regime-conditional by design (researcher resolution 2).", "Hallucination is a 4-component battery; primary = out-of-reference-support + valence/sanitization invalidity, secondary/exploratory = unmakeable/synthesability-undefined and target-agnostic repeats; the surrogate-to-independent-rescoring transfer gap is a mandatory reward-hacking diagnostic (researcher resolution 3).", "Default anchor is a single well-established receptor; the multi-target panel is an optional extension arm and the primary endpoint is fully evaluatable without it; named PDB targets are marked illustrative, not mandated (researcher resolution 4).", "Controls A6 (matched-output-count post-hoc top-k filter) and A7 (shuffled/identity reward placebo) are retained as load-bearing, and A2-vs-A5 provides the feedback-vs-diversity-mechanism separation (researcher resolution 5).", "Analysis carries a pre-registered joint primary endpoint, Pareto reporting, paired seeds, multiple-testing correction and bootstrap CIs; every grid value and threshold is labeled a proposed design parameter (researcher resolution 6).", "Generator, RDKit/Mordred, Vina/smina, trained affinity surrogate, independent scoring function, reference corpora, receptor grid and SA/fingerprint assets are external provisions absent from this workspace and are consolidated into one required-provisions list (researcher resolution 7).", "CPU-only execution: docking is confined to an audit/optional tier (<=60k calls study-wide) with training as the budget-limiting tier; no experiment was executed and no outcome, effect size or arm success is claimed or predicted."], "uncertainties": ["Whether the source intends a specific feedback injection mechanism; if later fixed, the E1/E2/E3 factor collapses to one arm and the grid shrinks, but A6/A7/transfer-gap controls remain valid.", "Whether R-BIO as primary alignment matches the source's notion of 'real-world'; if R-MK were primary, long-chain artifact verdicts invert for the same molecules - reported as a regime-interaction outcome rather than hidden.", "Docking runtime is assumed ~2 s/ligand and RDKit/SA throughput assumed cacheable; actual cost depends on ligand size, protonation/tautomer prep overhead and version-specific Vina behavior, so the compute ceiling may need pre-registered contraction.", "The diversity floor f_div can penalize diversity-mechanism arms; mitigated by sensitivity sweep and raw-score reporting, but the primary verdict's robustness to f_div is unknown a priori.", "Single-target anchoring leaves target-agnostic-repeat hallucination detection underpowered unless the optional panel extension is funded.", "Availability and fidelity of a trained affinity surrogate is unverified; if absent, affinity feedback must move to the docking-in-loop arm at much higher cost, changing the feasible grid size.", "Novelty and support thresholds (NN-Tanimoto < 0.4, central-95% bands, composite cut tau_c) are proposed values that must be frozen from a pilot before any run to avoid post-hoc tuning."]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-1fead9f7-d456-405b-8ded-bddc1c211bcf", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Complete design-only experiment: feedback-factor grid, truncation/placebo controls, dual-regime alignment, joint endpoint", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
